# The build context is source only. Host build output is the important
# exclusion: bin/ and obj/ here are Windows artefacts, and letting them into a
# Linux image gives the container a half-built tree that restores against the
# wrong RID and fails in ways that look like code problems.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
.git/
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/

# Not source, and no reason to rebuild the image when they change.
*.md

# Except this one, which stopped being documentation and became an input.
# DECISIONS 060 gave the log an index and a test that compares the two, so the
# suite reads DECISIONS.md at run time and the test image has to contain it.
# Without this line the four DecisionLogTests fail in the container with
# FileNotFoundException while passing on the host, which reads the real tree.
!DECISIONS.md
docker-compose.yml
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# The load harness is mounted into the k6 container at run time and is never built
# into an image. Its summaries are measurements that grow with every run, and
# uploading them to the daemon as build context is pure cost.
load/
